{"title":"1974 AHSME Problems/Problem 26","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of distinct positive integral divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/2/9c272995323d3bb2d05ac61745b0d38864436f97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(30)^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"19\" /> excluding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/2/9c272995323d3bb2d05ac61745b0d38864436f97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(30)^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"19\" /> is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/e/7ee45b01e95a0f46aa42421bf1f9a6f7ae3210b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)\\ } 100 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }125 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\  } 123 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\  } 30 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\  }\\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"492\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a9f060b3889b4124e72220ab8303e4c9f287a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot3\\cdot5$\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" />, so the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/c/4dc4852d69ae91d51f8f0fdc8541a8c0c7b0f51f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^4$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/0/0a00ec2ed38ca4d27e295a72c33dff06b0ccfe42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4\\cdot3^4\\cdot5^4$\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore, the number of positive divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/c/4dc4852d69ae91d51f8f0fdc8541a8c0c7b0f51f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^4$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/f/79faf2a023cb758ae9af2ce4d47ecf6cafe413ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4+1)(4+1)(4+1)=125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"214\" height=\"18\" />. However, we have to subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to account for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/c/4dc4852d69ae91d51f8f0fdc8541a8c0c7b0f51f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^4$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />, so our final answer is $ 125-2=123, \\boxed{\\text{C}} \n</p><p><br />\nsoln by RNVAA\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"mar